import{_ as o,o as t,c as a,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-004 — One OutputPass per composer; colour textures sRGB, data maps linear","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-004-one-outputpass-per-composer.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-004-one-outputpass-per-composer.md"}'),r={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-004-one-outputpass-per-composer.md"};function c(n,e,d,i,l,u){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="uxd-004-—-one-outputpass-per-composer-colour-textures-srgb-data-maps-linear" tabindex="-1">UXD-004 — One OutputPass per composer; colour textures sRGB, data maps linear <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-004-—-one-outputpass-per-composer-colour-textures-srgb-data-maps-linear" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-004 — One OutputPass per composer; colour textures sRGB, data maps linear&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted. The Fly Mars descent look is accepted &quot;for now&quot; after the second pass (plan line 460).</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-11 (proposed and decided)</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator — &quot;Surface colour pipeline (OutputPass) → now, 0.9.9 (operator 2026-11-11). Extended to every composer + sRGB tagging of all colour textures&quot; (<code>docs/wip/2026-11-11-0.9.9-plan.md</code> line 46); &quot;operator decision: one OutputPass per composer&quot; (<code>docs/wip/2026-11-11-ux-feedback-plan.md</code> lines 456–458); brief <code>docs/wip/2026-11-11-slice-output-step-brief.md</code> line 3 (&quot;Operator: /iss and /tiangong get the OutputPass; the rule is project-wide&quot;)</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: E2 and FY1 (scenes too dark) in part; slice &quot;output-step&quot;</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>docs/adr/TA.md</code> §composer pipeline and colour (line 371); <code>src/lib/three/README.md</code> (colour pipeline); <code>docs/guides/fly-cinematic-shot-language.md</code>, <code>fly-cinematic-gap-analysis.md</code>; AGENTS.md &quot;Performance — 3D scene discipline&quot;.</li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Composer render targets are linear. The renderer&#39;s <code>toneMapping</code> and <code>outputColorSpace</code> apply only when drawing to the canvas, so a scene rendered through an <code>EffectComposer</code> without a final OutputPass showed linear values (darker, more contrasty) and ignored its ACES setting, while direct-render tiers showed ACES plus sRGB (output brief lines 5–10). The surface composer was fixed first (commit <code>8e9a7c8d1d9</code>: <code>#889fe7</code> read as rgb 63,88,204 and now reads 136,156,228, <code>docs/wip/2026-11-09-0.9.9-redesign.md</code>). The output brief found six more composer chains without the pass: <code>/iss</code> and <code>/tiangong</code>, <code>/explore</code> solar, Milky Way and Local Group, <code>/fly</code> helio, and <code>/fly</code> launch, coast and descent (brief lines 12–22).</p><h2 id="options" tabindex="-1">Options <a class="header-anchor" href="#options" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Options&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The sources record the extension to every composer as the operator&#39;s decision and do not list alternatives. Not recorded: any option to keep a composer without the pass.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every <code>EffectComposer</code> chain <strong>ends in one OutputPass</strong> (after vignette, film and bokeh), which applies the renderer&#39;s tone mapping, exposure and sRGB once. Colour textures (albedo, emissive, sprite and label art) are tagged <strong><code>SRGBColorSpace</code></strong>; data maps (masks, height, normal and other non-colour data) stay linear and say so with an explicit <strong><code>NoColorSpace</code></strong>. Hex <code>Color</code> constants are already sRGB-aware.</p><p><strong>Status of the look.</strong> The rule is accepted. After the before/after sheets the operator said &quot;I agree we should fix washed out look on launches and descents&quot; (operator 2026-11-11, <code>docs/wip/2026-11-11-ux-feedback-plan.md</code> line 459). That line records a second pass in the same slice (atmosphere shell, sky gradient, ambient light, launch exposure) and says &quot;descent contrast still under review&quot;. The operator then accepted the descent after the second pass &quot;for now&quot; (contrast can be revisited later; operator go, 2026-11-11, plan line 460). Operator context from the brief: Explore (E2) and Fly 2D (FY1) were already &quot;too dark&quot;, so a lighter result is welcome, tuned so glow and bloom do not blow out (brief lines 43–44).</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Constants tuned against linear output (exposure, lights, emissives, bloom, vignette, film) are re-checked per scene; the brief lists them (lines 35–42).</li><li>Before/after screenshots per scene are the look check; the operator approves.</li><li>Rules out adding a composer without the pass, and a colour texture without a colour space.</li></ul><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>src/lib/three/output-step-rule.test.ts</code> (run <code>npx vitest run src/lib/three/</code>: 21 files, 189 tests passed, 2026-11-11):</p><ul><li><strong>A (per chain):</strong> each <code>EffectComposer</code> chain has exactly one <code>new OutputPass(</code>, and it is the last <code>addPass</code>/<code>insertPass</code> call; six composer sites. Mutation-checked: a duplicated pass and a pass moved before bloom both fail.</li><li><strong>B:</strong> both <code>createOutlinePassSetup({</code> users pass <code>outputPass: true</code>.</li><li><strong>C (per variable):</strong> every texture creation (<code>CanvasTexture</code>/<code>Texture</code>/<code>DataTexture</code>, any <code>.load(</code> on a TextureLoader, chained or variable-bound) tags the variable it creates, or the callback parameter, within 14 lines; the four data maps carry <code>NoColorSpace</code>. Mutation-checked, including <code>const tx = new THREE.TextureLoader(); tx.load(...)</code>.</li><li><strong>Shader colours:</strong> the composer scenes and their shader files (ascent, descent, helio and its overlays and mission, cislunar overlays, solar, Milky Way, Local Group, point-field) pass colours as <code>THREE.Color</code>: no <code>vec3</code>/<code>vec4</code> colour literals other than 0 and 1, no array or non-Color colour uniforms. Allow-listed with reasons: the black-hole shader (direct render, tone-maps itself) and one point-field whitening term. Mutation-checked on each branch.</li></ul><p><code>src/lib/three/outline-pass-setup.test.ts</code> (helper ends with one OutputPass) and <code>texture-colour-space.test.ts</code> (built stations, skydome, flare, hero maps) cover the builders.</p><p>e2e, production build of a9d0ccea983, <code>--workers=1</code>, desktop-chromium, mobile-chromium and mobile-landscape-chromium, specs iss, tiangong, explore, explore-milky-way, fly, fly-launch, fly-descent, fly-cislunar, fly-render-validation, visual: 324 passed, 0 failed, 114 skipped.</p><p>Slice commits: <code>78ca77e3fab</code> (composers, 53 textures, first retune), <code>9fdf4cc4a6b</code> (docs), <code>2adb8d7aa02</code> (moon texture tag, check A and C hardening), <code>55d3acfabed</code> (launch and descent wash-out fix, shader-colour guard), <code>2ae64cf6a0a</code> (exposure value in the shot-language guide), and the commit that carries this text (guard extended, TA/README/UXD updated). <code>fly-cinematic-gap-analysis.md</code> was touched in <code>9fdf4cc4a6b</code> (status note under the pass table).</p><p>No visual baseline covers a 3D canvas, so the look rests on the operator-reviewed before/after sheets. Real-GPU and Safari rendering were not checked.</p>',18)])])}const m=o(r,[["render",c]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
